v class=\"message\">Frankly I don't think werewolves think in a way that would be considered &quot;neurotypical&quot; anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I think first edition notes in many places that from the lead-up to the First Change and afterwards they are not what humans would consider normal in behavior. With the variety of wolf-blooded Tells there's probably a lot of other diagnoses you could slap on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T13:11:28-07:00","id":1107728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1107540-autism-and-uratha?p=1107698#post1107698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what stimming is. Is it to calm oneself, or to get you familiar stimulation?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stimming\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Black_and_Indigenous_Autistic_Non-binary_Person_Playing_with_Tangle.jpg/1280px-Black_and_Indigenous_Autistic_Non-binary_P